    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17851" root="زف" body-key="z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زَفِيفٌ</span></b>  (S, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَزَفُّ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِفَّانِىٌّ</span></b> , (Ibn-'Abbád, K,) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">زِفَّانٌ</span></b> , without <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ى</span>, (L, TA,) <i>Quick,</i>
(Ibn-'Abbád, S, L, K,) like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذَفِيفٌ</span>, (S,) and <i>light.</i>
(L, TA. [In the CK the explanation is omitted.]) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  It is also an inf. n.: (S, K, &amp;c.:) or a simple
subst. (Msb.) [See 1, in several places.)

